apply('en/index.html', '    <p class="parr">Stone, paper and code follow the same path. A path that asks you to decide nothing leaves your attention free, and that has become hard to come by. Hence the book’s subtitle, and hence the countdown: a labyrinth fable for loud days.</p>\n  </div></div>\n</section>\n<a class="pilar a" href="/en/labyrinth/"><span class="n">01</span><h3>Los Escullos</h3><span class="glo">The walkable labyrinth · Cabo de Gata-Níjar</span><span class="fl">→</span></a>\n', '    <p class="parr">Stone, paper and code follow the same path. A path that asks you to decide nothing leaves your attention free, and that has become hard to come by. Hence the book’s subtitle, and hence the countdown: a labyrinth fable for loud days.</p>\n  </div></div>\n</section>\n<section class="tramo env" id="cabo-de-gata">\n  <span class="rot">Cabo de Gata</span>\n  <h2 class="grande">From one path, a wider landscape.</h2>\n  <div class="dos"><div>\n    <p class="parr">OOLITA will remain one labyrinth at Los Escullos. Around that path, the project is growing into field publications, textile editions and collaborations that help children and adults look more closely at Cabo de Gata.</p>\n    <p class="parr">Next will come field books for family visits, experiments with natural colour, and work with local makers around material traditions such as pita fibre.</p>\n  </div><div>\n    <p class="parr">The aim is not to bring more people to one point. It is to support slower visits, local knowledge and care for the living landscape.</p>\n  </div></div>\n</section>\n<a class="pilar a" href="/en/labyrinth/"><span class="n">01</span><h3>Los Escullos</h3><span class="glo">The walkable labyrinth · Cabo de Gata-Níjar</span><span class="fl">→</span></a>\n')
