apply('en/editions/index.html', '  "name": "Editions — objects born of OOLITA",\n  "description": "The book and the t-shirt born of the Los Escullos labyrinth: two editions made one at a time, when you ask for them. Book 31.01.27, t-shirt 28.03.27.",\n', '  "name": "Editions — books, textiles and tools for looking closely · OOLITA",\n  "description": "The book and T-shirt are the first OOLITA editions: a series growing into field publications, textile works and collaborations rooted in Cabo de Gata.",\n')
apply('en/editions/index.html', '<h1 class="grande">Objects born of OOLITA.</h1><p class="lema">And they <em>travel with you</em>.</p><p class="lema-en" lang="es">Objetos que nacen de OOLITA — y viajan contigo</p><p class="glosa">A book and a t-shirt. They come from the Los Escullos labyrinth and are made one at a time, when you ask for them. Two releases, two moments, one story.</p><p class="parr">Both are made on demand: nothing is produced before someone wants it, there is no warehouse, and no copy and no size is left over. Each piece is made after the order, at the workshop nearest its destination, so it travels very little.</p><p class="parr">The book comes out on 31 January 2027, a month after the three-dimensional labyrinth opens. The t-shirt arrives on 28 March, once the design has finished being revealed Sunday by Sunday. That order — walk it first, own it after — is the order of the whole work.</p><p class="parr">Neither one is a souvenir. They are the labyrinth in other materials — paper that opens flat on a table, cotton that goes out into the street — the way the three-dimensional world is the labyrinth in code. The stone stays at Los Escullos; these are the forms that know how to travel.</p><h2 class="rot">The book and the t-shirt</h2>\n', '<h1 class="grande">Books, textiles and tools for looking closely.</h1><p class="lema">The first <em>editions</em>.</p><p class="lema-en" lang="es">Libros, textiles y herramientas para mirar de cerca</p><p class="glosa">The book and T-shirt are the first OOLITA editions. They begin a wider series of field publications, small textile works and collaborations rooted in Cabo de Gata.</p><p class="parr">Each edition will state who made it, where it was made, what materials were used and how many were produced. Each piece is produced only after it is ordered, avoiding unsold stock. Production and delivery details are stated separately for every edition.</p><p class="parr">The book comes out on 31 January 2027. The first textile edition follows on 28 March, once its design has been revealed Sunday by Sunday.</p><p class="parr">Neither is a souvenir. The book carries the path into paper; the first textile edition carries it into cloth. Future editions will look beyond the path to the wider territory around it.</p><h2 class="rot">First editions</h2>\n')

